> Q14.

```{r}
library(ggplot2)
ggplot(data, aes(x = geno, y = exp, fill = geno)) + geom_boxplot() + labs(title = "Gene Expression by Genotype (eQTL rs8067378)", x = "Genotype", y = "Expression Level") + theme_minimal() + theme(legend.position = "none")
```
The plot above suggests that there is reduced expression in the G|G genotype compared to the A|A genotype. Given the distributions of G|G compared to A|A, I would think that there is a reduction in expression of ORMDL3 in G|G individuals, but I have not performed a statistical test that sufficiently shows a difference between the two groups.

